{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer","id":1007789,"title":"An evil Record Producer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-24T11:59:15-08:00","id":1007789,"title":"An evil Record Producer","content":"I am thinking about getting C20 when it comes out and I have a question. I already came up with an antagonist who runs a record label. I want to know how I can make him fit in Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:24:39-08:00","id":1007802,"title":"","content":"It depends, really. What role do you want him to play?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:33:14-08:00","id":1007806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007802#post1007802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends, really. What role do you want him to play?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda like a big boss type character. My storyline starts off when one of the Changelings rescues a human relative who happens to be a musician who was being exploited by the producer. The producer, wanting him back, sends people after them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:37:30-08:00","id":1007810,"title":"","content":"Is the antagonist a changeling? If so, he could be using the label as a way of finding Dreamers to Ravage, preying on one generation of hopefuls after another for Glamour and cranking out one-hit wonders to fill his wallet at the same time. If you're seeing it as more of an Autumn Person, then he could be making sure that everything that the label puts out fits neatly into a set formula of what works to appeal to the lowest common denominator and crushing any attempts at creativity or originality in favor of constant rehashes of the same shallow things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T12:52:06-08:00","id":1007814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007810#post1007810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the antagonist a changeling? If so, he could be using the label as a way of finding Dreamers to Ravage, preying on one generation of hopefuls after another for Glamour and cranking out one-hit wonders to fill his wallet at the same time. If you're seeing it as more of an Autumn Person, then he could be making sure that everything that the label puts out fits neatly into a set formula of what works to appeal to the lowest common denominator and crushing any attempts at creativity or originality in favor of constant rehashes of the same shallow things.</div> </div> </div> </div>He is a Autumn Person. He could be doing rehashed songs. But I also picture him being the type of guy who exploits his musicians by going back on his word multiple times and paying them less than the contract specified. Also, does the hiring thugs to track them down part sound too dark for Changeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-24-2016, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T14:19:46-08:00","id":1007839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007814#post1007814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He is a Autumn Person. He could be doing rehashed songs. But I also picture him being the type of guy who exploits his musicians by going back on his word multiple times and paying them less than the contract specified. Also, does the hiring thugs to track them down part sound too dark for Changeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Changeling can be quite dark. Things to keep in mind, though, is that he'd probably have some way of covering his ass if he's going to hire thugs. If he's going to be an effective boss enemy, then he'll need to know how to keep himself out of legal trouble. He'd probably be less likely to go back on the letter of the contract, and more likely to exploit loopholes in the legalese. For example, instead of paying less than the amount specified, he'd probably point out fees owed to the label or penalties associated with certain activities. Going back on his spoken word works well, as long as there's no recordings of what he's said around. I'd play up his money, too. Give him some highly paid lawyers and a few choice corrupt police officers in his pocket. If he does get taken to court, he plays it off so that many court dates are needed, eventually bankrupting whoever is trying to sue him just from legal fees. Those are just a few thoughts I had about it.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for posting this up here. Thinking about this has inspired a whole story for the world-hopping game that I'm currently running for my wife, and she's already quite excited just from the little bit that I've shared with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T15:16:29-08:00","id":1007854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007839#post1007839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not at all. Changeling can be quite dark. Things to keep in mind, though, is that he'd probably have some way of covering his ass if he's going to hire thugs. If he's going to be an effective boss enemy, then he'll need to know how to keep himself out of legal trouble. He'd probably be less likely to go back on the letter of the contract, and more likely to exploit loopholes in the legalese. For example, instead of paying less than the amount specified, he'd probably point out fees owed to the label or penalties associated with certain activities. Going back on his spoken word works well, as long as there's no recordings of what he's said around. I'd play up his money, too. Give him some highly paid lawyers and a few choice corrupt police officers in his pocket. If he does get taken to court, he plays it off so that many court dates are needed, eventually bankrupting whoever is trying to sue him just from legal fees. Those are just a few thoughts I had about it.<br /> <br /> Also, thank you for posting this up here. Thinking about this has inspired a whole story for the world-hopping game that I'm currently running for my wife, and she's already quite excited just from the little bit that I've shared with her.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a good idea and I will take your suggestions. Also, you are planning on using the producer in a chronicle? I am okay with that. Also, is their a way for changelings to fight back against thugs or any other human enemy my guy throws at them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T16:13:41-08:00","id":1007866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007854#post1007854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a good idea and I will take your suggestions. Also, you are planning on using the producer in a chronicle? I am okay with that. Also, is their a way for changelings to fight back against thugs or any other human enemy my guy throws at them?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's plenty that a changeling can do, depending on kith and Arts/Realms. If the characters are creative, they can use a lot of the powers to defend themselves. Without knowing the characters, I can't give specific examples that would be necessarily relevant to your situation.<br /> <br /> I will be using an evil producer for the next story, although I dare say that it will be much different from yours. In mine, the character will be entering a world where such a character will have managed to regulate all the creativity out of music in an effort to eradicate the &quot;mental illness &quot; of changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T18:55:17-08:00","id":1007903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007866#post1007866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's plenty that a changeling can do, depending on kith and Arts/Realms. If the characters are creative, they can use a lot of the powers to defend themselves. Without knowing the characters, I can't give specific examples that would be necessarily relevant to your situation.<br /> <br /> I will be using an evil producer for the next story, although I dare say that it will be much different from yours. In mine, the character will be entering a world where such a character will have managed to regulate all the creativity out of music in an effort to eradicate the &quot;mental illness &quot; of changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCan I provide you with a hypothetical scenario where a group of NPC changelings are attacked by a group of thugs sent by the producer and you can show me how they fight back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-24-2016, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T19:59:53-08:00","id":1007914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007903#post1007903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bCan I provide you with a hypothetical scenario where a group of NPC changelings are attacked by a group of thugs sent by the producer and you can show me how they fight back?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. I'd need to know kiths, Arts, and Realms for the changelings and weapons and tactics of the thugs, but I'm sure I could come up with something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T20:30:41-08:00","id":1007920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007914#post1007914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Absolutely. I'd need to know kiths, Arts, and Realms for the changelings and weapons and tactics of the thugs, but I'm sure I could come up with something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it make sense if one of the members of the changeling group is a Sidhe? Also, the human relative is gonna be related to either a Satyr or a Boggan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-25-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T22:47:38-08:00","id":1007956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007920#post1007920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it make sense if one of the members of the changeling group is a Sidhe? Also, the human relative is gonna be related to either a Satyr or a Boggan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could make perfect sense, if the sidhe has a good reason to hang around with the commoners. Really the characters just need a plausible backstory to make that work. One possibility would be for the characters to have been friends before they ever learned that they were changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T06:55:21-08:00","id":1008060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1007956#post1007956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It could make perfect sense, if the sidhe has a good reason to hang around with the commoners. Really the characters just need a plausible backstory to make that work. One possibility would be for the characters to have been friends before they ever learned that they were changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThem being friends actually makes perfect since. Also, I decided to make the human relative related to the Boggan character because it would makes since for a kith that has a compulsion to help others to help one of his relatives. Also, here is the appearance of the Record Producer <a href=\"https://thumbs.dreamstime.com/z/businessman-evil-look-16415064.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://thumbs.dreamstime.com/z/busi...k-16415064.jpg</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bAnd this the appearance of one of the thugs you will encounter in the scenario. <a href=\"http://i.istockimg.com/file_thumbview_approve/6335873/2/stock-photo-6335873-thug.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.istockimg.com/file_thumbvie...35873-thug.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:22:13-08:00","id":1008073,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">When I saw the topic of this thread, I immediately thought of Suge Knight as a redcap.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T07:40:09-08:00","id":1008081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008073#post1008073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">When I saw the topic of this thread, I immediately thought of Suge Knight as a redcap.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI looked him up on Wikipedia after you posted that. I can see why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:24:03-08:00","id":1008099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008060#post1008060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThem being friends actually makes perfect since. Also, I decided to make the human relative related to the Boggan character because it would makes since for a kith that has a compulsion to help others to help one of his relatives. Also, here is the appearance of the Record Producer <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;https://thumbs.dreamstime.com/z/businessman-evil-look-16415064.jpg&amp;quot;\" target=\"_blank\">https://thumbs.dreamstime.com/z/busi...k-16415064.jpg</a> <br /> <br /> \u200bAnd this the appearance of one of the thugs you will encounter in the scenario. <a href=\"http://i.istockimg.com/file_thumbview_approve/6335873/2/stock-photo-6335873-thug.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://i.istockimg.com/file_thumbvie...35873-thug.jpg</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so we have a sidhe, a boggan, and a satyr against thugs with crowbars. What Arts and Realms do they have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T08:46:12-08:00","id":1008108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008099#post1008099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, so we have a sidhe, a boggan, and a satyr against thugs with crowbars. What Arts and Realms do they have?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sidhe has Wayfare and Prop<br /> The Boggan has Chicanery and Actor<br /> The Satyr has Soothsay and Nature<br /> \u200bAlso, I will post the introduction to the scene and will control the human relative and thugs while you control the Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:14:07-08:00","id":1008212,"title":"","content":"Okay, sounds interesting. I'm assuming starting characters with 3 dots in each Art and 5 in the chosen Realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T11:36:50-08:00","id":1008222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008212#post1008212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, sounds interesting. I'm assuming starting characters with 3 dots in each Art and 5 in the chosen Realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. Also the fight is gonna take place in a restaurant after you get the relative out of the recording studio. Also, the thugs will not be wearing the kind of masks in the appearance. Finally, what do you think of the producer's appearance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:01:03-08:00","id":1008231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008222#post1008222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. Also the fight is gonna take place in a restaurant after you get the relative out of the recording studio. Also, the thugs will not be wearing the kind of masks in the appearance. Finally, what do you think of the producer's appearance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Appearance seemed fine to me. Restaurant seems a rather public place for such a thing. I'm assuming that it's being disguised as a robbery? If not, you'll need to give some thought to how the producer is keeping himself distanced from it. Is the restaurant a freehold or is it just an ordinary restaurant? Is it crowded? Are the changelings worrying about revealing themselves as such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T12:13:15-08:00","id":1008234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008231#post1008231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Appearance seemed fine to me. Restaurant seems a rather public place for such a thing. I'm assuming that it's being disguised as a robbery? If not, you'll need to give some thought to how the producer is keeping himself distanced from it. Is the restaurant a freehold or is it just an ordinary restaurant? Is it crowded? Are the changelings worrying about revealing themselves as such?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I will move the setting to the relative's house and make it look like a burgularly. Also, would a sidhe just pull out a sword at the thugs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T14:22:48-08:00","id":1008271,"title":"","content":"Depends on the sidhe, and whether or not they have a sword and willingness to use it. Same goes for any kith, really. If they're trying to get the law on their side, they probably wouldn't want to leave a trail of bodies, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T15:49:41-08:00","id":1008301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008271#post1008271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the sidhe, and whether or not they have a sword and willingness to use it. Same goes for any kith, really. If they're trying to get the law on their side, they probably wouldn't want to leave a trail of bodies, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I will try to post the opening. Also, is it bad that I am picturing a illustration of my record producer scowling while a black mist is coming from his body? The mist is actually a physical form of banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T17:10:15-08:00","id":1008327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008301#post1008301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, I will try to post the opening. Also, is it bad that I am picturing a illustration of my record producer scowling while a black mist is coming from his body? The mist is actually a physical form of banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing wrong with depicting banality as a black mist in the eyes of the changelings. My wife suggested that a rusty color could be good for that, too. It's really however you want to do it in your game. In my case, I'd probably have something more subtle, like the vibrancy of colors fading when he is near, with similar subtle &quot;dimming&quot; of the other senses. One of the best things about Changeling: The Dreaming is that you can kind of let your imagination go nuts, even for the characters that would crush that very imagination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T18:12:28-08:00","id":1008353,"title":"","content":"<br /> Reno, Nevada<br /> \u200bIt has been a few hours since you took your cousin and fled from the Bullion Records building. As a Boggan, you felt like it was your duty to help when your cousin told you about the unscrupulous behavior of John Macady, the producer in charge of the company. At first, you asked him why He could not leave by himself and sue him. Your cousin then dropped a bombshell when he told you that John would not let him leave due to a loophole in the contract that stated that he had to stay for all the 5 years he agreed to in the contract. So, you immediately went to Reno along with your childhood friends, Rachel, a sidhe, and Carter, a Satyr.<br /> <br /> \u200bGetting your cousin out of the building was a hard task however. It turns out that John did not want to let go of his new investment and you and your motley had to fight your way through Bullion Security to get out of the building. But, you managed to get out of the building and fled to your cousin's house in the suburbs. The house however, was neglected due to the fact that the contract provided your cousin with an apartment in the Bullion building. Unsurprisingly, the electricity was cut and so was the gas and water. You are currently in the house getting ready to leave town in the morning. Your cousin is in his old room strumming his guitar and humming a melody, Rachel is in the backyard staring at the stars while Carter is in the living room, reading a magazine. You, were in the second bedroom in the house, packing yours and everyone else's bags for the morning.<br /> <br /> You suddenly hear a window break. You immediately stop packing and go investigate. As you walk through the hall you hear noises coming from the bathroom. You go up to the door and peek through a crack in the door. You see a broken window and a few shards of broken glass. Suddenly, a man wearing a ski mask pokes his head through the window and looks around as if trying to see if anyone was around. After a few moments of looking around, the man started to climb through the broken window. The man was tall, thin and wore blue jeans, a red shirt and a leather jacket. After getting in the room, he stuck his hand up and helped a smaller looking burglar wearing the same clothes in. A few more men climbed in, one was more portly then the other two and the final man was muscular. There were four burglars in total, all of them wearing ski masks. The tall man, obviously the leader, said to them in a hushed voice that had a hint of a Hispanic accent,&quot; Remember, we came here for the musician. The boss said not to hurt anyone unless absolutely necessary&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bYou try to sneak away from the door to warn your cousin and your friends. But, right before you reach the foot of the stairs you trip on a rag. You land with a loud thud. You hear footsteps running towards you, the burglars have heard you. &quot; Well, well, well&quot;, the muscular burglar said,&quot; looks like we got a witness.&quot; Luckily, your seeming keeps the burglars from seeing what you really look like. But, it can't save you from being beaten up. The portly burglar cackles as he walks up to you cracking his knuckles. When he gets close enough, he tries to punch you in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T07:52:38-08:00","id":1008535,"title":"","content":"Okay, so, we've got one boggan with Chicanery and Actor against four thugs. While the boggan does have backup nearby, they won't be there in time to save him from being whomped by the thugs. Worse, the poor bastard is already down, so he can't even flee. He's getting hit here, and there's not much he can do to avoid it. He probably should have called for help at the first sign of the intrusion, but at this point, it's too late for that. He does have Actor 5, which means that he can cast cantrips directly on the attackers, but the only Art he has access to is Chicanery. There's precious little that the boggan to do to make this a fair fight, much less one in his favor. The best he can hope to do is buy some time and hope that his other changeling friends heard the breaking glass and are coming to investigate as well. Since he knows that the thugs are hoping to avoid a scene, he can also hope that they'll run at the first sign that something's wrong. He uses Chicanery on the closest thug, making him perceive the sound of his cousin practicing the guitar as police sirens pulling up outside the house. If he had Scene as well, he could have attempted to make all of the thugs hear it, but since he doesn't, he has to hope that the one will be enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T08:08:34-08:00","id":1008540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008535#post1008535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so, we've got one boggan with Chicanery and Actor against four thugs. While the boggan does have backup nearby, they won't be there in time to save him from being whomped by the thugs. Worse, the poor bastard is already down, so he can't even flee. He's getting hit here, and there's not much he can do to avoid it. He probably should have called for help at the first sign of the intrusion, but at this point, it's too late for that. He does have Actor 5, which means that he can cast cantrips directly on the attackers, but the only Art he has access to is Chicanery. There's precious little that the boggan to do to make this a fair fight, much less one in his favor. The best he can hope to do is buy some time and hope that his other changeling friends heard the breaking glass and are coming to investigate as well. Since he knows that the thugs are hoping to avoid a scene, he can also hope that they'll run at the first sign that something's wrong. He uses Chicanery on the closest thug, making him perceive the sound of his cousin practicing the guitar as police sirens pulling up outside the house. If he had Scene as well, he could have attempted to make all of the thugs hear it, but since he doesn't, he has to hope that the one will be enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe thug suddenly says to his buddies,&quot; Guys, the cops are here!&quot; The short thug turns and says to him in a confused voice,&quot; What are you talking about?&quot; The portly thug stops hitting the boggan and says,&quot; Come on dude, I hear no sirens. You're crazy.&quot; Suddenly, your cousin appears, guitar in hand. He lets out a gasp of horror when he see the burglars. The muscular one turns and says to him,&quot; Well, well. If it isn't Bill Thatcher. We have been hired to come get you.&quot; The muscular burglar then ran up the stairs to grab Bill. But, Bill managed to bash the burglar on the head with his guitar. As the burglar fell down the stairs, he made loud thudding noises that echoed throughout the house. You can hear the sound of clopping hoofs. Carter has heard the noise and is going to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-26-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T09:23:24-08:00","id":1008578,"title":"","content":"Carter has a couple options open to him. Running for help may be the best choice, since Rachel has the best magical options to get them all out of this alive. We can get to her later, though, because I believe the goal to this exercise is to see what each one can do individually. Soothsay is his only Art, and at three dots, it doesn't give him a whole lot of combat options. With Nature being his only Realm, it takes all utility out of his cantrips to try and fight these guys with him. Calling upon the Wyrd is a good choice, at this point. It will allow him to move at his full speed, and since he still has the element of surprise, he may be able to charge into one of them, using his horns to hit his target hard and fast. Some satyr characters I've had have also taken advantage of people's superstitious natures to impersonate the Devil when calling upon the Wyrd, encouraging them towards negative behaviors so that they can get ahold of souls, which usually has the effect of people running in terror and seriously reconsidering their paths in life. Sometimes they react with violence, though, so it's always a risk. Soothsay is associated with blessings and curses as well as prophecy, though, and C20 is giving changelings the option of Unleashing an Art, so let's go with that. Carter calls upon the Soothsay Art, says &quot;Save my friends,&quot; and Unleashes. We'll assume he's coaxing the Wyrd rather than commanding, so that gives him a much easier time succeeding, but less control over the outcome. What could happen here? A few thoughts off the top of my head: The thug punching the boggan might end up missing, hitting the something hard instead and shattering his fist, his resulting scream distracting the others enough for the protagonists to regroup together. Or, maybe it turns out that a neighbor had heard the strumming of the guitar earlier, called the cops for a noise complaint, and they are just now arriving. Or, the thugs begin getting visions of their fate if they continue on their current course of action, and begin to have a change of heart. Of course, Unleashing can always end up going a bit awry if the character is too successful. Perhaps the thugs gain visions of an apocalyptic scenario, and realize that this small group of changelings are the ones destined to stop it. Instead of beating them down and taking the musician, they realize that they must protect the world's last hope, and found a cult to do just that. Naturally, the vision they saw would be completely true, and Carter Unleashing Soothsay has now conscripted him and his friends into the role of heroes, whether they like it or not. The best part about Unleashing, especially when coaxing, is that you can tie it into the rest of your story pretty easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T09:42:46-08:00","id":1008582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_poste