 might end up missing, hitting the something hard instead and shattering his fist, his resulting scream distracting the others enough for the protagonists to regroup together. Or, maybe it turns out that a neighbor had heard the strumming of the guitar earlier, called the cops for a noise complaint, and they are just now arriving. Or, the thugs begin getting visions of their fate if they continue on their current course of action, and begin to have a change of heart. Of course, Unleashing can always end up going a bit awry if the character is too successful. Perhaps the thugs gain visions of an apocalyptic scenario, and realize that this small group of changelings are the ones destined to stop it. Instead of beating them down and taking the musician, they realize that they must protect the world's last hope, and found a cult to do just that. Naturally, the vision they saw would be completely true, and Carter Unleashing Soothsay has now conscripted him and his friends into the role of heroes, whether they like it or not. The best part about Unleashing, especially when coaxing, is that you can tie it into the rest of your story pretty easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am probably gonna go with the portly thug smashing his fist on something.<br /> \u200bThe portly thug in blind anger turned to hit you once more. But, you took advantage of the distraction your cousin caused to sneak away, causing the thug to hit part of the stairs. As the portly thug grabbed his wrist and cursed, the other thugs all turned to check on their buddy. This gave you and Carter a chance to get Rachel. The short thug however, notices Carter and charges at him with his crowbar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","user":"Killerclown","date":". 11-26-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T10:53:47-08:00","id":1008609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/413818-ctd-reality-check-moderizing-without-risking-banality\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/413818-ctd-reality-check-moderizing-without-risking-banality\"> CtD: Reality Check - Moderizing without risking Banality. - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/413818-ctd-reality-check-moderizing-without-risking-banality\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/413818-ctd-reality-check-moderizing-without-risking-banality </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Going a bit backwards with my history project for CtD. Modernization. While most of the Courts and various subfactions and Motleys struggle with modernizing. Grumps want to stick with the old ways like the old farts they are; Childings love the whimzie and the pageantry like a social outcast at a ren-fair. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> This was my base idea for moderizing changelings. Haven't done much for Unseelie musicicians or producers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:21:14-08:00","id":1008693,"title":"","content":"So, Rachel's turn now. Wayfare is a bit more useful, as far as cantrips go. With only Prop to call upon, though, I'd imagine that the extra actions available from Level 2 won't be doing anyone any good. Level 1, though, could prove useful, as the thug's weapon or clothing could be made to leap. Without Scene, though, she can only go after one at a time. That means that if she's going to end this quickly, she's going to have to pull out the big guns and Unleash Wayfare. Once again, we'll assume coaxing rather than commanding, as success in the moment is the most important thing. &quot;Stop our foes from harming any of us,&quot; she says, letting the magic pour through her. The most likely outcome here would be for either the thugs or the characters to end up elsewhere. If it goes out of control, though, they could end up somewhere very interesting indeed, even if they're safe from their enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:25:35-08:00","id":1008696,"title":"","content":"Like end up in some kind of casino? Also, John Macaedy is probably gonna be pissed that they escaped and send more people after them. If i could make this a globe trotting campaign how do you think it work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T15:43:59-08:00","id":1008700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008696#post1008696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like end up in some kind of casino? Also, John Macaedy is probably gonna be pissed that they escaped and send more people after them. If i could make this a globe trotting campaign how do you think it work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Any destination works, as long as it's safe from their enemies. The producer would naturally be furious about their escape, but as an Autumn Person, he will never believe any reports of something supernatural happening. You'll need to give some thought of just what it is that the musician has to offer to make it worth his effort to keep coming after him, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T16:20:30-08:00","id":1008711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008700#post1008700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. Any destination works, as long as it's safe from their enemies. The producer would naturally be furious about their escape, but as an Autumn Person, he will never believe any reports of something supernatural happening. You'll need to give some thought of just what it is that the musician has to offer to make it worth his effort to keep coming after him, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two reasons. One, He violated his contract by leaving early and John hates it when people violate hos contract. Or he has a great singing voice that sells a lot of records. Possibly because he is a kin of some other changeling. Also, John will possibly send a Dauntain after them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T17:54:39-08:00","id":1008725,"title":"","content":"One thing you could do is have it be that the character technically fulfilled all of his contractual obligations already, but the producer got someone to forge his signature to extend the contract for five more years. With enough &quot;witnesses&quot; that claim to have seen him sign the papers, he might have few legal options to utilize, thus making his escape the only option left to him. For all intents and purposes, it would seem that John was legally in the right, given that his illegal activities occur outside of the public eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T18:12:28-08:00","id":1008728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1007789-an-evil-record-producer?p=1008725#post1008725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing you could do is have it be that the character technically fulfilled all of his contractual obligations already, but the producer got someone to forge his signature to extend the contract for five more years. With enough &quot;witnesses&quot; that claim to have seen him sign the papers, he might have few legal options to utilize, thus making his escape the only option left to him. For all intents and purposes, it would seem that John was legally in the right, given that his illegal activities occur outside of the public eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds good and I will use it. Also, one part of the story could have the characters show up in a police station trying to get John arrested. But, to there horror, the detective they are talking to and two policemen were bought out by John and get the changelings arrested for filing a false report. Also, does the Dautain henchman idea make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":